==Latin==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|la|cōdex}}

===Etymology===
Uncertain, but some have connected it to {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₃osk-||ash tree}}, the same source as Welsh {{m|cy|onnen}}, Latin {{m|la|ornus||wild mountain ash}}, Lithuanian {{m|lt|úosis}}, Russian {{m|ru|я́сень}}, Albanian {{m|sq|ah||beech}}, Ancient Greek {{term|ὀξύα||beech|lang=grc}}, Old Armenian {{term|հացի|lang=xcl}}. The connection stems from the assumption that Indo-Europeans used hollowed out ash trees as boats and skiffs.<ref>Schrader, Prehistoric antiquities of the Aryan peoples: a manual of comparative philology and the earliest culture</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|caudex}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|caudex||caudicis|m|third}}

# A [[tree trunk]], [[stump]].
# A [[bollard]]; [[post]].
# A [[book]], [[writing]]; [[notebook]], [[account book]].
# {{context|pejorative|lang=la}} A [[blockhead]], [[idiot]].

